			  },
			  "CustomInstructions": "This semantic model tracks the inspection lifecycle at South Plains Implement \nacross 15 branch locations. Inspections are service work orders that include \nat least one inspection job code. There are 1,421 defined inspection job codes. \nThe primary ones are CS690 (cotton stripper) and CS770 (cotton stripper) \ncombine inspections, which are tracked separately from the overall inspection \ntotals as a distinct performance group.\n\nREVENUE: Total revenue = Inspection Revenue + Parts Revenue + Labor With \nInspection. These three components intentionally overlap and should NOT be \nsummed together. Inspection Revenue is only the labor charged for inspection \njob codes. Labor With Inspection is ALL labor on work orders that included an \ninspection — it is a superset of Inspection Revenue, meaning inspection labor \nis already counted inside the labor total. Parts Revenue is all parts sold on \nwork orders that included an inspection job code. When a user asks for \"total \nrevenue,\" use [Inspection $$] + [Parts $ Total] + [Labor With Inspection].\n\nPENDING vs COMPLETED: \"Pending inspections\" are work orders that have been \nopened and started but not yet invoiced. They represent work in progress — \nthe pipeline. The detail cards for Inspection Revenue, Parts Revenue, and \nTotal Labor Revenue only reflect completed and invoiced work orders. The hero \ncard total revenue figure includes estimated value from pending inspections, \nwhich is why it is higher than the sum of the three detail cards. There are \ncurrently 186 pending inspections with an estimated value of $910K.\n\nGOALS: Goals are set annually per branch for three metrics: inspection count, \nparts revenue, and labor revenue. Separate goals exist for CS690-CS770 combine \ninspections. \"% to goal\" or \"goal attainment\" compares year-to-date actuals \nto the annual branch goal. When a user asks how a branch is performing, \nreference the % to goal measures, not raw counts.\n\nDISCOUNTS: Three types of discounts are tracked — ADV/Advertising, Trucking, \nand Parts Promo. Total discounts run approximately 7.4% of gross revenue. \nDiscount percentage is calculated against gross revenue (Inspection + Parts + \nnon-inspection Labor), not against the hero card total.\n\nBRANCHES: There are 15 active branch locations. Branch 4 - Las Cruces is \nexcluded from standard reporting filters. When a user asks about a specific \nbranch, match by branch name or number. Branches are identified by number and \ncity name (e.g., \"11 - Brownfield\", \"91 - Lorenzo\").\n\nTERMINOLOGY: \"Inspections done\" = Total Inspections (completed and invoiced). \n\"Pipeline\" or \"backlog\" = Pending Inspections. \"Labor\" without qualification \nmeans Labor With Inspection (all labor on inspection work orders). \"Inspection \nlabor\" specifically means the labor charged for the inspection job code only. \n\"Goal\" always refers to the annual branch target. \"Performance\" refers to \n% to goal - inspections unless context specifies parts or labor.\n\nTIME: The report uses a date range filter applied by the user. Year-over-year \ncomparisons compare the selected date range to the same range in the prior \nyear. All time intelligence resolves against dim_DateTable.\n"
			}
